1
00:00:01,543 --> 00:00:03,503
[KOUSUKE] The average
eroge protagonist tends to live

2
00:00:03,587 --> 00:00:05,839
what many would view
as an enviable life.

3
00:00:06,590 --> 00:00:09,343
[both grunting]

4
00:00:10,802 --> 00:00:11,929
[grunts]

5
00:00:13,722 --> 00:00:15,140
Mentors to guide you,

6
00:00:15,807 --> 00:00:17,059
heroines who adore you,

7
00:00:17,601 --> 00:00:19,895
and the concrete chance
for a happy ending.

8
00:00:19,978 --> 00:00:22,314
It's exactly the life
players wish they could have.

9
00:00:23,023 --> 00:00:24,358
I mean, the games are designed

10
00:00:24,441 --> 00:00:25,943
to be escapist fantasy,
after all.

11
00:00:26,026 --> 00:00:26,944
[door opens]

12
00:00:27,027 --> 00:00:28,654
[MARINO] Good morning, Kou.

13
00:00:29,321 --> 00:00:31,740
Would you be a dear
and wake up Hatsumi for me?

14
00:00:31,823 --> 00:00:32,783
Sure.

15
00:00:33,075 --> 00:00:35,202
So, what about
the sidekick character?

16
00:00:35,911 --> 00:00:38,747
Eroge normally finds
their misery hilarious.

17
00:00:39,581 --> 00:00:42,251
Hey, Hatsumi, wake up.
Your breakfast is getting cold.

18
00:00:42,918 --> 00:00:43,919
[snores softly]

19
00:00:45,879 --> 00:00:47,089
It's time to get up now.

20
00:00:47,172 --> 00:00:49,299
You're gonna be late
for class if-- [gasps]

21
00:00:49,383 --> 00:00:50,801
[exclaiming]

22
00:00:51,593 --> 00:00:53,136
[whimpers]

23
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:55,764
[HATSUMI] Come on,
call me "big sis."

24
00:00:55,847 --> 00:00:56,723
[gasps]

25
00:00:58,141 --> 00:00:59,893
[KOUSUKE] This sidekick,
on the other hand,

26
00:00:59,977 --> 00:01:02,938
I'd say I've got it just
as good as any protagonist.

27
00:01:03,021 --> 00:01:04,481
Seems that way, at least.

28
00:01:06,692 --> 00:01:07,609
Right?

29
00:01:10,028 --> 00:01:12,781
[♪ opening theme song playing]

30
00:02:40,869 --> 00:02:42,746
[school bell chiming]

31
00:02:44,081 --> 00:02:46,625
-Well, it's dungeon time.
-Mm.

32
00:02:46,708 --> 00:02:48,919
[students chattering]

33
00:02:49,002 --> 00:02:51,546
Hey, class is about to start.

34
00:02:51,630 --> 00:02:53,131
[KOUSUKE]
I'm not worried about it.

35
00:02:53,215 --> 00:02:55,509
-I've attended enough days.
-But... Hang on!

36
00:02:57,511 --> 00:03:00,097
Is he really
skipping class again?

37
00:03:00,722 --> 00:03:02,099
Sure looks like it.

38
00:03:02,182 --> 00:03:04,601
[student 1 scoffs] Damn him,
making Ludivine worry.

39
00:03:04,685 --> 00:03:06,770
[STUDENT 2] Does he know
how lucky he is to be here?

40
00:03:06,853 --> 00:03:08,647
[STUDENT 3] It's like
he wants to be a loser.

41
00:03:08,730 --> 00:03:11,733
[STUDENT 4] Why come here
if he doesn't wanna learn magic?

42
00:03:12,442 --> 00:03:15,237
Any particular dungeon
you want us to explore, Master?

43
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:18,073
Sure is. There's a certain skill
I wanna obtain.

44
00:03:18,990 --> 00:03:21,368
But we actually need to get
permission for this crawl.

45
00:03:22,035 --> 00:03:23,662
-[RUIJA] Mr. Takioto!
-[gasps]

46
00:03:24,329 --> 00:03:26,164
[KOUSUKE] Oh, Ms. Ruija!

47
00:03:26,248 --> 00:03:29,042
Jeez, you're not even subtle
about skipping!

48
00:03:29,126 --> 00:03:30,168
You're coming with me

49
00:03:30,252 --> 00:03:31,586
-right this instant!
-[KOUSUKE] Huh?

50
00:03:33,171 --> 00:03:35,382
[RUIJA] I'm so glad
I caught you before you left.

51
00:03:36,174 --> 00:03:38,677
I don't really care
how you spend your days,

52
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:40,637
but Hatsumi
spoke to me privately

53
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:42,597
regarding
your performance inadequacy

54
00:03:42,681 --> 00:03:44,474
when it comes to emission magic.

55
00:03:44,558 --> 00:03:45,559
[KOUSUKE] She did?

56
00:03:46,143 --> 00:03:48,645
[chuckles] She was a grade
below me during her time here.

57
00:03:48,728 --> 00:03:51,440
We went dungeon diving
together all the time.

58
00:03:51,523 --> 00:03:52,858
[KOUSUKE] Wow, I had no idea.

59
00:03:52,941 --> 00:03:56,236
Well, it's true. Wait,
Hatsumi never mentioned it?

60
00:03:56,319 --> 00:03:58,738
Hatsumi doesn't really mention
much of anything.

61
00:03:58,822 --> 00:03:59,906
Good point.

62
00:04:00,365 --> 00:04:01,700
But when it came
to the subject of you,

63
00:04:01,783 --> 00:04:03,285
she was downright voluble.

64
00:04:03,702 --> 00:04:04,661
And I have something here

65
00:04:04,744 --> 00:04:07,205
-she asked me to borrow for you.
-Uh?

66
00:04:08,957 --> 00:04:10,417
Ta-da!

67
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:12,419
It's a mana-measuring device,
look!

68
00:04:12,502 --> 00:04:14,963
Really? A tool to measure mana?

69
00:04:15,922 --> 00:04:18,216
The shape strikes me
as a little sinister.

70
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:20,510
[KOUSUKE] Yeah. What's with
the horns on the sides?

71
00:04:20,594 --> 00:04:21,511
[RUIJA] I dunno.

72
00:04:22,179 --> 00:04:24,723
[KOUSUKE] Right, and why is it
decorated with human skulls?

73
00:04:24,806 --> 00:04:25,807
[RUIJA] I dunno.

74
00:04:26,099 --> 00:04:27,517
[KOUSUKE]
And why are some of the switches

75
00:04:27,601 --> 00:04:29,561
-already flipped on?
-[RUIJA] I dunno.

76
00:04:29,644 --> 00:04:31,146
[KOUSUKE]
I have an urgent appointment.

77
00:04:31,229 --> 00:04:32,856
[RUIJA] No! Please don't leave!

78
00:04:32,939 --> 00:04:34,024
[straining]

79
00:04:34,107 --> 00:04:35,275
I myself was struck

80
00:04:35,734 --> 00:04:37,569
with the same ominous sense
of dread when I first saw it,

81
00:04:37,652 --> 00:04:39,571
but I assure you
it's perfectly safe!

82
00:04:39,654 --> 00:04:40,780
I'll have you know I borrowed it

83
00:04:40,864 --> 00:04:42,240
from the school's
most brilliant inventor,

84
00:04:42,324 --> 00:04:43,992
so if she says it's safe,
it's safe!

85
00:04:44,075 --> 00:04:45,285
[giggles] Probably.

86
00:04:46,411 --> 00:04:48,580
And they know this because
they already tested it, right?

87
00:04:48,663 --> 00:04:50,373
[RUIJA] Uh...

88
00:04:50,457 --> 00:04:53,001
[KOUSUKE] Can you tell me
who this brilliant inventor is?

89
00:04:53,084 --> 00:04:55,879
[RUIJA] She's an upperclassman,
so I doubt you would know her,

90
00:04:55,962 --> 00:04:57,506
but her name's Anemone.

91
00:04:59,257 --> 00:05:00,800
You should trust me on this.

92
00:05:01,259 --> 00:05:02,844
-Please return it.
-[gasps]

93
00:05:02,928 --> 00:05:04,179
You tell me I should trust you

94
00:05:04,262 --> 00:05:06,223
when you have
that little faith in me?!

95
00:05:07,224 --> 00:05:08,266
[KOUSUKE] Hmm.

96
00:05:08,725 --> 00:05:11,311
Anemone's a side heroine
you're guaranteed to befriend

97
00:05:11,394 --> 00:05:12,354
in the game,

98
00:05:12,979 --> 00:05:15,690
referred to by some players as
"the mad-sexy scientist."

99
00:05:15,774 --> 00:05:18,151
She is a genius,
it's true, but--

100
00:05:18,902 --> 00:05:20,987
Don't you think
you should test it out first?

101
00:05:21,071 --> 00:05:23,198
[RUIJA] Not possible.
She loaned it to me

102
00:05:23,281 --> 00:05:24,699
after I consulted her
on your condition,

103
00:05:24,783 --> 00:05:27,536
saying it was the perfect thing
for you specifically.

104
00:05:28,328 --> 00:05:30,038
And she promised me
she would keep her mouth shut

105
00:05:30,121 --> 00:05:32,374
if I bring back
the results of the test for her.

106
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:34,584
-[KOUSUKE] Shut about what?
-[gasps]

107
00:05:34,668 --> 00:05:36,336
[gasps] Uh!

108
00:05:36,419 --> 00:05:38,046
Did I say... I mean, um...

109
00:05:38,755 --> 00:05:39,714
[KOUSUKE] That's right.

110
00:05:40,048 --> 00:05:41,508
I forgot blackmail
made up a large part

111
00:05:41,591 --> 00:05:43,385
of her character arc
in the game.

112
00:05:43,677 --> 00:05:44,719
[groans]

113
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:46,888
Something wrong, Master?

114
00:05:46,972 --> 00:05:49,266
Fine, let's get this over with.

115
00:05:49,349 --> 00:05:52,018
But only if you tell me
the dirt Anemone has on you.

116
00:05:52,102 --> 00:05:54,187
What? No!
I couldn't possibly tell you.

117
00:05:54,271 --> 00:05:55,647
I mean,
she doesn't have any dirt.

118
00:05:55,730 --> 00:05:57,524
What dirt?
There isn't anything to tell!

119
00:05:57,607 --> 00:05:59,317
[KOUSUKE]
Your relationship with Ms. Ruija

120
00:05:59,401 --> 00:06:01,278
develops on a side quest
in the game

121
00:06:03,071 --> 00:06:04,406
And it's not in the classroom,

122
00:06:05,156 --> 00:06:07,284
but a shop
in the red-light district.

123
00:06:08,243 --> 00:06:11,705
The idea to go sexploring
comes from Kousuke, of course.

124
00:06:11,788 --> 00:06:14,457
And that's where Iori has
a surprise encounter with...

125
00:06:17,502 --> 00:06:18,420
[gasps]

126
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:23,842
[gasps]

127
00:06:25,594 --> 00:06:28,054
[KOUSUKE] The game skipped
over a lot of details,

128
00:06:28,138 --> 00:06:29,598
but she apparently
took on the work

129
00:06:29,681 --> 00:06:31,850
because she was
in desperate need of money.

130
00:06:32,684 --> 00:06:35,103
The devs might've added
a patch to flesh out her story

131
00:06:35,186 --> 00:06:37,439
if she'd been more popular
with the players.

132
00:06:37,522 --> 00:06:40,817
But as it is, we're left
with the broad strokes.

133
00:06:41,860 --> 00:06:44,404
Hmm. I have a hunch
what's going on,

134
00:06:44,487 --> 00:06:46,573
but you're telling us
if I do this.

135
00:06:46,656 --> 00:06:48,366
I told you,
there's nothing to tell!

136
00:06:48,450 --> 00:06:50,619
-That's enough.
-I'm sorry, it's a deal.

137
00:06:51,453 --> 00:06:52,954
It's fine. I get it.

138
00:06:53,038 --> 00:06:55,123
Now let's just fire up
this infernal machine

139
00:06:55,206 --> 00:06:56,541
and do this already.

140
00:06:56,625 --> 00:06:58,752
-But once the test is done--
-[gasps] Okay!

141
00:06:58,835 --> 00:07:02,005
Um, you really feel comfortable
using this thing?

142
00:07:02,088 --> 00:07:05,300
I wouldn't say comfortable,
but it is gonna help me, right?

143
00:07:05,383 --> 00:07:07,802
I'd like to know what's wrong
with my emission magic.

144
00:07:09,179 --> 00:07:12,265
So, uh,
why do I have to be fully naked?

145
00:07:12,349 --> 00:07:15,060
[NANAMI] Because the manual's
quite insistent on it.

146
00:07:15,143 --> 00:07:16,811
[Ruija gasping]

147
00:07:16,895 --> 00:07:18,063
Oh, wow.

148
00:07:18,563 --> 00:07:20,940
[NANAMI] Now we attach
the electrodes to your body.

149
00:07:21,024 --> 00:07:22,609
Me! Let me! I can help!

150
00:07:24,361 --> 00:07:25,528
Hmm.

151
00:07:28,823 --> 00:07:31,785
-Can we please hurry this along?
-Of course! I'm sorry!

152
00:07:31,868 --> 00:07:33,036
[both exclaim]

153
00:07:33,662 --> 00:07:35,622
[KOUSUKE] Is this the game
rewarding me here?

154
00:07:35,705 --> 00:07:38,375
Oh, man, this is about to
get noticeably bad!

155
00:07:38,458 --> 00:07:39,751
[RUIJA] I'm so sorry!

156
00:07:39,834 --> 00:07:41,711
Can you please
take over, Nanami?

157
00:07:41,795 --> 00:07:44,422
[NANAMI] Of course.
I'll just turn it on.

158
00:07:44,506 --> 00:07:46,424
[machine whirring]

159
00:07:46,508 --> 00:07:50,887
[Kousuke screaming]

160
00:07:50,971 --> 00:07:52,555
[machine sputtering]

161
00:07:52,639 --> 00:07:54,974
[RUIJA] Oh,
please tell me you're all right.

162
00:07:55,558 --> 00:07:57,811
Physically, sure, I'm fine,

163
00:07:57,894 --> 00:08:00,397
but my mental state
is hanging on by a loose thread.

164
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:01,648
[RUIJA] I'm terribly sorry,

165
00:08:01,731 --> 00:08:03,483
but the good news is
we were at least able

166
00:08:03,566 --> 00:08:04,984
to get a data printout,
so there's that.

167
00:08:05,068 --> 00:08:06,027
-[booms]
-[Ruija yelps]

168
00:08:06,653 --> 00:08:08,947
Looks like you're made of
tougher stuff than the machine.

169
00:08:09,030 --> 00:08:11,574
[KOUSUKE]
Always listen to your instincts.

170
00:08:11,658 --> 00:08:13,743
I knew
Anemone's invention was sketchy.

171
00:08:15,829 --> 00:08:17,789
Find any answers in there?

172
00:08:17,872 --> 00:08:19,124
Well, more or less.

173
00:08:19,207 --> 00:08:20,375
From what I can gather,

174
00:08:20,750 --> 00:08:22,836
there must be some kind
of internal factor blocking you

175
00:08:22,919 --> 00:08:26,005
from releasing the magic
before it can materialize.

176
00:08:26,089 --> 00:08:29,259
Or maybe it could be
an external interference.

177
00:08:29,342 --> 00:08:31,886
No matter what
the cause may be, it's amazing

178
00:08:31,970 --> 00:08:34,305
that you can contain
this much mana within you.

179
00:08:34,389 --> 00:08:35,724
The real mystery is

180
00:08:35,807 --> 00:08:37,684
how your body
can hold that amount.

181
00:08:37,976 --> 00:08:39,310
Is it really that high?

182
00:08:39,394 --> 00:08:40,603
But it might not be

183
00:08:40,687 --> 00:08:42,939
that your internal amount
is abnormal,

184
00:08:43,023 --> 00:08:46,192
but that it's somehow stored
outside your body instead.

185
00:08:46,276 --> 00:08:47,318
And if that's the case,

186
00:08:47,736 --> 00:08:50,363
it would seem to lend credence
to Hatsumi's theories

187
00:08:50,447 --> 00:08:53,324
of extra-dimensional
mana proliferation and storage.

188
00:08:53,408 --> 00:08:54,617
-But if that's true...
-Do you think

189
00:08:54,701 --> 00:08:56,745
this muttering
is building to a solution?

190
00:08:56,828 --> 00:08:57,829
Good question.

191
00:08:57,912 --> 00:08:58,788
[gasps]

192
00:08:59,539 --> 00:09:01,332
[squeals]

193
00:09:01,416 --> 00:09:02,834
Amazing!

194
00:09:02,917 --> 00:09:04,502
This data
might very well hold the key

195
00:09:04,586 --> 00:09:06,212
to a groundbreaking discovery!

196
00:09:06,296 --> 00:09:09,174
It could even end up making it
into the history books!

197
00:09:09,257 --> 00:09:11,634
That's awesome. Keep me updated
on what you find.

198
00:09:11,718 --> 00:09:14,053
But let's set it down for now.

199
00:09:14,137 --> 00:09:16,431
Time for you to honor
your end of the deal.

200
00:09:16,973 --> 00:09:18,183
Deal?

201
00:09:18,266 --> 00:09:19,684
[sobs]

202
00:09:19,768 --> 00:09:22,479
-That's a lot of debt.
-[RUIJA] I'm well aware!

203
00:09:22,562 --> 00:09:24,189
All right,
just to get this straight,

204
00:09:24,272 --> 00:09:26,900
you're flat broke
due to debt and back taxes,

205
00:09:26,983 --> 00:09:29,611
which led you to being evicted
and squatting here.

206
00:09:29,694 --> 00:09:31,154
Hoping to turn things around,

207
00:09:31,237 --> 00:09:33,948
you decided to take a side job
in the red-light district,

208
00:09:34,032 --> 00:09:35,867
but Anemone found out about it.

209
00:09:35,950 --> 00:09:37,118
Ever since that happened,

210
00:09:37,202 --> 00:09:38,703
she's been threatening
to expose you

211
00:09:38,787 --> 00:09:40,413
unless you do
whatever she wants.

212
00:09:40,830 --> 00:09:41,915
[RUIJA] Exactly.

213
00:09:42,373 --> 00:09:45,126
-May I see the loan contract?
-[RUIJA] There isn't one.

214
00:09:45,210 --> 00:09:47,420
But they gave me
their assurance that it'd be

215
00:09:47,504 --> 00:09:49,172
a stress-free
monthly payment plan

216
00:09:49,255 --> 00:09:50,757
that anyone could easily afford.

217
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:53,176
Yeah,
you're clearly being scammed.

218
00:09:53,259 --> 00:09:55,011
-[RUIJA] Huh?
-Why did you let your debt

219
00:09:55,095 --> 00:09:56,679
-pile up so high?
-[gasps]

220
00:09:56,763 --> 00:09:58,807
You're the adult here, you know!

221
00:09:58,890 --> 00:10:00,892
You can't
be this irresponsible forever!

222
00:10:00,975 --> 00:10:03,645
I'm pathetic, I know! [cries]

223
00:10:03,728 --> 00:10:06,397
[KOUSUKE] Yeah,
I'd cry in her situation too.

224
00:10:06,481 --> 00:10:09,192
She's getting lectured
on her finances by a student.

225
00:10:10,193 --> 00:10:12,737
So, what are you planning
to do here, Master?

226
00:10:12,821 --> 00:10:14,656
-[KOUSUKE] Only one thing to do.
-[Ruija crying]

227
00:10:18,243 --> 00:10:19,869
Hey, Marino, got a sec?

228
00:10:19,953 --> 00:10:21,621
[RUIJA]
The principal? She'll fire me!

229
00:10:23,456 --> 00:10:25,166
[Marino, Kousuke sigh]

230
00:10:25,250 --> 00:10:26,417
[sniffles]

231
00:10:26,501 --> 00:10:28,169
I'm surprised
that you haven't resorted

232
00:10:28,253 --> 00:10:29,796
to selling your organs by now.

233
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:31,798
[KOUSUKE] It took us some work,

234
00:10:31,881 --> 00:10:33,842
but we managed
to reduce Ms. Ruija's debt

235
00:10:33,925 --> 00:10:34,801
by a good amount.

236
00:10:35,885 --> 00:10:37,303
It required a lawyer,

237
00:10:37,387 --> 00:10:39,305
the Hanamura family's
tax attorney.

238
00:10:39,973 --> 00:10:42,725
Not to mention the rather tense
in-person negotiations

239
00:10:42,809 --> 00:10:44,477
with some scary-looking dudes.

240
00:10:45,270 --> 00:10:46,271
[sighs]

241
00:10:46,729 --> 00:10:49,524
As for the remainder
of the debt, it's in the hands

242
00:10:49,607 --> 00:10:51,860
-of the Hanamura family now.
-[Ruija gasps]

243
00:10:52,235 --> 00:10:55,196
You couldn't dream up a safer
and more honest creditor.

244
00:10:55,280 --> 00:10:58,366
In all seriousness,
if you were some random teacher,

245
00:10:58,449 --> 00:10:59,868
I would've fired you
on the spot.

246
00:11:00,743 --> 00:11:03,371
You can thank Kousuke
and your solid track record.

247
00:11:03,454 --> 00:11:06,082
Oh, thank you!
I'm so deeply grateful!

248
00:11:06,875 --> 00:11:08,960
[MARINO] But I cannot
allow you to live on campus.

249
00:11:09,586 --> 00:11:10,920
So you're moving
into an apartment

250
00:11:11,004 --> 00:11:12,422
in one of our properties.

251
00:11:12,505 --> 00:11:13,798
I'll simply see that the rent

252
00:11:13,882 --> 00:11:16,009
and debt payments
are deducted from your salary.

253
00:11:16,092 --> 00:11:17,594
-Huh?
-[MARINO] It'll take about

254
00:11:17,677 --> 00:11:20,847
ten years to pay off, unless
you make some drastic changes.

255
00:11:20,930 --> 00:11:21,973
Ten years, huh?

256
00:11:22,056 --> 00:11:24,183
Uh-huh. Math doesn't lie.

257
00:11:24,267 --> 00:11:26,519
[MARINO] Furthermore,
I've determined she needs

258
00:11:26,603 --> 00:11:28,313
to be under a conservatorship.

259
00:11:28,396 --> 00:11:31,357
Yeah, best to play it safe.

260
00:11:31,733 --> 00:11:33,610
The mess she made for herself,

261
00:11:33,693 --> 00:11:35,987
she clearly needs
someone watching over her.

262
00:11:36,070 --> 00:11:38,281
She's just so freaking gullible.

263
00:11:38,740 --> 00:11:40,158
Glad you agree.

264
00:11:40,241 --> 00:11:41,910
'Cause you'll be
in charge of that, Kou.

265
00:11:41,993 --> 00:11:44,454
Yeah, that makes sense--
Wait, what?!

266
00:11:44,537 --> 00:11:46,831
The deed to the apartment
has already been transferred

267
00:11:46,915 --> 00:11:48,082
to your name.

268
00:11:48,166 --> 00:11:49,959
The deed to the entire building,
that is.

269
00:11:50,043 --> 00:11:52,587
Seriously?
Well, that's cool with me!

270
00:11:52,670 --> 00:11:54,047
Hold on, this isn't cool at all!

271
00:11:54,130 --> 00:11:56,007
No, it's cool. Right?

272
00:11:56,090 --> 00:11:57,175
Mm.

273
00:11:57,717 --> 00:12:00,178
Please sign here to yield
all financial control to Master.

274
00:12:01,304 --> 00:12:02,513
[RUIJA] Okidoki!

275
00:12:02,597 --> 00:12:03,890
You're not even gonna read it?!

276
00:12:03,973 --> 00:12:06,100
That's exactly how
you got into this whole mess!

277
00:12:06,184 --> 00:12:08,061
Ah! I'm so relieved.

278
00:12:08,144 --> 00:12:10,647
I can finally sleep in peace,
and in a bed too.

279
00:12:10,730 --> 00:12:12,398
-[humming]
-[KOUSUKE] I'm glad to hear it.

280
00:12:12,482 --> 00:12:14,233
But please work hard
to pay off the debt.

281
00:12:14,317 --> 00:12:16,110
[Ruija chuckles]
Of course I will!

282
00:12:16,194 --> 00:12:19,948
Oh, wait, I just remembered.
Can I ask you for a favor?

283
00:12:20,949 --> 00:12:21,824
Hmm?

284
00:12:23,701 --> 00:12:24,869
[birds chirping]

285
00:12:28,998 --> 00:12:30,541
I don't understand, Master.

286
00:12:30,625 --> 00:12:32,251
Why waste time
on a beginner dungeon

287
00:12:32,335 --> 00:12:33,753
when you're so far beyond it?

288
00:12:34,921 --> 00:12:36,047
Waste of time?

289
00:12:36,464 --> 00:12:38,508
Not if you're planning on
pulling an RTA.

290
00:12:38,591 --> 00:12:39,884
Of course, I see.

291
00:12:39,968 --> 00:12:41,636
So you're after
a special reward.

292
00:12:41,719 --> 00:12:43,680
I knew a Dungeon Maid
would get it.

293
00:12:46,683 --> 00:12:48,142
[BOTH] Huh?

294
00:12:48,226 --> 00:12:49,519
-[KOUSUKE] Let's move!
-[NANAMI] Right!

295
00:12:49,602 --> 00:12:51,437
♪

296
00:12:51,521 --> 00:12:52,730
[KOUSUKE] Fighting trash mobs

297
00:12:52,814 --> 00:12:54,941
defeats the entire purpose
of an RTA.

298
00:12:56,567 --> 00:12:57,735
The objective is
to speed through

299
00:12:57,819 --> 00:12:59,737
-to the end, not gain XP.
-[goblin growls]

300
00:13:00,488 --> 00:13:03,199
So you ignore the threats
and move on to the next level.

301
00:13:04,659 --> 00:13:05,994
[bats whooshing]

302
00:13:06,911 --> 00:13:08,454
[Nanami panting]

303
00:13:08,913 --> 00:13:11,624
-Sorry, just a moment.
-Oh, don't worry. You're fine.

304
00:13:13,209 --> 00:13:15,003
In the game,
there's no need for any rest.

305
00:13:15,086 --> 00:13:17,046
You simply rush
through the dungeon,

306
00:13:17,130 --> 00:13:18,339
but this is for real.

307
00:13:18,881 --> 00:13:21,342
So you run out of breath,
your legs feel like jelly...

308
00:13:22,510 --> 00:13:24,095
...and there's a good chance
you might get ambushed

309
00:13:24,178 --> 00:13:25,888
since you're only focused
on moving forward.

310
00:13:25,972 --> 00:13:27,015
[Nanami sighs]

311
00:13:27,598 --> 00:13:29,058
[KOUSUKE] Looks like we should
slow down for a minute.

312
00:13:31,102 --> 00:13:33,980
-Nanami, are you okay?
-Yeah.

313
00:13:34,063 --> 00:13:35,565
Are we going to make it in time?

314
00:13:36,357 --> 00:13:37,984
[KOUSUKE] One hour, 25 minutes.

315
00:13:38,067 --> 00:13:40,862
Oh, yeah! We'll definitely
make it in time.

316
00:13:41,654 --> 00:13:44,032
Your only chance
of entering the special floor,

317
00:13:44,115 --> 00:13:46,576
Layer 10, is to make it there
within one hour

318
00:13:46,659 --> 00:13:48,286
and 40 minutes at the most.

319
00:13:48,995 --> 00:13:50,371
And would you look at that?

320
00:13:50,455 --> 00:13:52,081
We've already pulled it off
with time to spare.

321
00:13:54,667 --> 00:13:57,170
[gasps] Wait,
is this a maze layer?

322
00:13:57,712 --> 00:13:59,380
I'll break it down while we run.

323
00:13:59,464 --> 00:14:00,757
-Are you ready?
-Mm.

324
00:14:01,758 --> 00:14:02,925
[KOUSUKE] The layout
for the special floor

325
00:14:03,009 --> 00:14:04,594
has eight unique paths to it.

326
00:14:04,677 --> 00:14:06,971
Each one has
its own forks and obstacles,

327
00:14:07,055 --> 00:14:09,515
and some even lead you
into a cruel infinity loop.

328
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:13,686
Can you memorize the turns
of the route we take?

329
00:14:13,770 --> 00:14:14,979
Of course I can.

330
00:14:16,606 --> 00:14:18,024
[Nanami panting]

331
00:14:18,691 --> 00:14:19,817
We first turned east,

332
00:14:19,901 --> 00:14:21,569
which led to
a four-way crossing.

333
00:14:21,652 --> 00:14:23,321
We then took the northern path,

334
00:14:23,404 --> 00:14:25,239
and hit a second
four-way crossing.

335
00:14:25,323 --> 00:14:26,324
[KOUSUKE] Good work!

336
00:14:26,616 --> 00:14:29,410
That settles it then.
We're on path D.

337
00:14:29,494 --> 00:14:30,578
From here,

338
00:14:30,661 --> 00:14:32,580
we have to follow
the route south,

339
00:14:32,663 --> 00:14:35,541
west, south, south,
east, and north.

340
00:14:38,669 --> 00:14:40,254
There! I knew we'd make it!

341
00:14:40,338 --> 00:14:43,925
-What's our time?
-[NANAMI] One hour, 56 minutes.

342
00:14:44,342 --> 00:14:46,094
[KOUSUKE] To claim the reward,
you have to clear

343
00:14:46,177 --> 00:14:47,845
the full dungeon
from the first floor

344
00:14:47,929 --> 00:14:49,764
to the final boss
within two hours.

345
00:14:53,184 --> 00:14:55,061
We've only got
four minutes left.

346
00:14:57,647 --> 00:14:59,565
-Stand back, I'll handle this.
-Nope.

347
00:14:59,649 --> 00:15:02,944
There's a much faster way
to defeat this guy, trust me.

348
00:15:04,320 --> 00:15:05,696
[grunts]

349
00:15:08,324 --> 00:15:10,535
[monster growls]

350
00:15:10,618 --> 00:15:12,036
What now, Master?

351
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:13,162
Stand back and watch!

352
00:15:13,746 --> 00:15:15,915
[yells]

353
00:15:22,839 --> 00:15:25,716
Awesome. That fight didn't even
eat up a full minute.

354
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:26,717
-[rumbling]
-[both gasp]

355
00:15:31,305 --> 00:15:32,557
[GODDESS STATUE] Well done.

356
00:15:32,640 --> 00:15:34,642
To defeat the evil
and stand here before me

357
00:15:34,725 --> 00:15:35,810
is an impressive feat.

358
00:15:36,644 --> 00:15:39,981
To reward your heroics,
I will grant you a skill.

359
00:15:43,359 --> 00:15:45,278
It appears
we were endowed with the spell

360
00:15:45,361 --> 00:15:47,405
-to increase stamina.
-Yup.

361
00:15:48,990 --> 00:15:50,533
[KOUSUKE]
There are five skill types,

362
00:15:50,616 --> 00:15:52,618
but the rewards
are always randomized.

363
00:15:53,161 --> 00:15:54,954
If you're aiming
to be the strongest,

364
00:15:55,037 --> 00:15:57,248
you need to acquire
each and every one of them.

365
00:15:58,207 --> 00:16:00,793
So we'll be back
for at least four more RTAs.

366
00:16:01,711 --> 00:16:04,797
All right, then! Let's test out
how much further we can run

367
00:16:04,881 --> 00:16:06,424
without getting winded now.

368
00:16:06,507 --> 00:16:08,551
I would suggest
another dungeon speed-run,

369
00:16:08,634 --> 00:16:10,386
but school's already let out.

370
00:16:10,470 --> 00:16:13,055
-Lucky for you, I have an idea.
-Huh?

371
00:16:15,183 --> 00:16:17,977
[NANAMI] Presenting
your very own treadmill!

372
00:16:18,060 --> 00:16:19,061
[ALL] Huh?

373
00:16:19,353 --> 00:16:22,106
Heavy rain, heavy snow,
typhoons, Nanami,

374
00:16:22,190 --> 00:16:23,482
no matter the conditions,

375
00:16:23,566 --> 00:16:26,110
you can comfortably run
whenever you want, Master.

376
00:16:26,194 --> 00:16:28,613
Did you count yourself
as a force of nature?

377
00:16:28,696 --> 00:16:32,074
Why not? I'm only a syllable off
from a "tsunami," you know.

378
00:16:32,575 --> 00:16:34,785
I'm gonna ignore
all of that and move on.

379
00:16:35,620 --> 00:16:37,371
[YUKINE] This looks like
a pretty fancy machine.

380
00:16:37,455 --> 00:16:39,665
There's something odd
about it, though.

381
00:16:39,749 --> 00:16:41,626
[NANAMI] I found an interesting
shop the other day,

382
00:16:41,709 --> 00:16:43,294
but I'd rather not say where.

383
00:16:43,377 --> 00:16:46,172
The bargain bin was stocked
with esoteric items.

384
00:16:46,255 --> 00:16:47,465
So I bought them,

385
00:16:47,548 --> 00:16:49,634
postulated the function
they might serve,

386
00:16:49,717 --> 00:16:51,844
and then I built this.
[chuckles smugly]

387
00:16:51,928 --> 00:16:55,139
Yeah, I didn't find this thing's
origin story very reassuring.

388
00:16:56,432 --> 00:16:58,684
[NANAMI] Why don't you go ahead
and give it a spin?

389
00:16:58,768 --> 00:17:00,895
It's incredibly easy to operate.

390
00:17:00,978 --> 00:17:04,148
The bad feeling I'm getting
from it is through the roof.

391
00:17:04,232 --> 00:17:05,775
But sure, why not give it a go?

392
00:17:05,858 --> 00:17:08,277
[LUDIVINE] Your bad feeling,
that's why not.

393
00:17:10,363 --> 00:17:11,697
[KOUSUKE] Press this?

394
00:17:12,532 --> 00:17:14,158
I went ahead
and took the initiative

395
00:17:14,242 --> 00:17:15,993
of completing
your user profile for you.

396
00:17:16,077 --> 00:17:19,288
Your name, gender,
physical stats, and whatnot.

397
00:17:19,705 --> 00:17:20,706
[KOUSUKE] Hmm?

398
00:17:20,790 --> 00:17:21,832
Now I'm worried about

399
00:17:22,375 --> 00:17:24,794
how you know my measurements
down to the precise decimals.

400
00:17:24,877 --> 00:17:28,422
It'll also update and log data
on your body fat percentage

401
00:17:28,506 --> 00:17:29,924
as well as
the calories you burn,

402
00:17:30,007 --> 00:17:33,010
which it then transfers
to your Tsukuyomi Traveler.

403
00:17:33,094 --> 00:17:34,679
Wow, that's useful.

404
00:17:34,762 --> 00:17:36,514
You've got me intrigued
to use it now.

405
00:17:36,597 --> 00:17:38,182
Yeah,
I'd like to try it out as well.

406
00:17:38,266 --> 00:17:40,017
I thought
that might be the case,

407
00:17:40,101 --> 00:17:42,603
so I've already registered
you all as users.

408
00:17:42,687 --> 00:17:44,772
You'll each be recognized
by the database.

409
00:17:44,855 --> 00:17:46,274
Before it will be possible

410
00:17:46,357 --> 00:17:47,608
for you to use
the machine though,

411
00:17:47,692 --> 00:17:49,485
everyone with the exclusion
of Master

412
00:17:49,569 --> 00:17:52,071
will have to first select
their main maid or butler.

413
00:17:52,154 --> 00:17:54,949
Why do we need a maid
or butler on a treadmill?

414
00:17:55,032 --> 00:17:57,201
To assist you
with your fitness goals.

415
00:17:57,285 --> 00:17:58,202
Such as this.

416
00:17:58,995 --> 00:18:00,288
[AUTOMATED VOICE]
Please use the touchscreen

417
00:18:00,371 --> 00:18:02,290
or voice commands
to make your choice.

418
00:18:02,373 --> 00:18:04,500
Oh, hey! Is that your voice?

419
00:18:04,583 --> 00:18:07,253
Well, do you have another
main maid that I am unaware of?

420
00:18:07,336 --> 00:18:10,006
And I went ahead and used
Master's voice as the template

421
00:18:10,089 --> 00:18:11,757
for the main butler option.

422
00:18:11,841 --> 00:18:14,260
[gasps] This sounds kinda fun!

423
00:18:14,802 --> 00:18:17,221
Right? It's a convenient feature
at the least.

424
00:18:17,763 --> 00:18:19,765
We'll start
by setting your target distance.

425
00:18:20,641 --> 00:18:22,518
The current default
is set just a smidge

426
00:18:22,601 --> 00:18:23,853
above 42 kilometers.

427
00:18:23,936 --> 00:18:25,229
[LUDIVINE] That's way too far!

428
00:18:25,313 --> 00:18:27,231
Isn't that a pretty
average distance?

429
00:18:27,315 --> 00:18:29,108
I normally run that far,
don't you?

430
00:18:29,191 --> 00:18:30,484
[laughs awkwardly]

431
00:18:30,568 --> 00:18:32,278
I have a feeling
that was set with you

432
00:18:32,361 --> 00:18:34,405
and Master Takioto in mind.

433
00:18:34,488 --> 00:18:35,698
Can it be set to zero?

434
00:18:36,532 --> 00:18:38,242
[Kousuke panting]

435
00:18:39,827 --> 00:18:40,786
Hmm?

436
00:18:41,537 --> 00:18:42,997
What do these buttons do?

437
00:18:43,539 --> 00:18:44,790
[NANAMI] In all honesty,

438
00:18:44,874 --> 00:18:47,293
I'm not entirely sure
what they're capable of,

439
00:18:47,376 --> 00:18:49,128
so please don't push them.

440
00:18:49,837 --> 00:18:52,006
[KOUSUKE] How are you not sure?
You built it.

441
00:18:52,089 --> 00:18:54,342
Yes, but I built it
with used items from a dungeon.

442
00:18:54,425 --> 00:18:55,760
-[HATSUMI] I have to know.
-[beeps]

443
00:18:55,843 --> 00:18:56,677
-[KOUSUKE] Wha--
-[Nanami gasps]

444
00:18:57,470 --> 00:19:00,222
Whoa! This thing isn't gonna
let me stop running!

445
00:19:00,806 --> 00:19:01,891
[panting]

446
00:19:01,974 --> 00:19:02,850
[Ludivine gasps]

447
00:19:02,933 --> 00:19:04,685
[all gasp]

448
00:19:05,311 --> 00:19:07,897
Why is this happening?!

449
00:19:07,980 --> 00:19:09,648
[NANAMI]
It's the Divine Wind mode.

450
00:19:09,732 --> 00:19:12,026
It generates wind
based on your running speed.

451
00:19:12,109 --> 00:19:13,903
It has three levels
of difficulty,

452
00:19:13,986 --> 00:19:16,530
violation, degradation,
and pure bliss.

453
00:19:16,614 --> 00:19:17,531
[KOUSUKE]
Of course the treadmill

454
00:19:17,615 --> 00:19:18,949
has a panty-flash mode!

455
00:19:19,033 --> 00:19:21,702
It's too much! No more!
I can't get off!

456
00:19:21,786 --> 00:19:23,120
Make it stop!

457
00:19:23,204 --> 00:19:25,373
Hit the stop button, Hatsumi!

458
00:19:28,125 --> 00:19:30,336
What the... [sighs]

459
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:32,421
[Ludivine sighs]

460
00:19:32,797 --> 00:19:34,173
[NANAMI] What's wrong?
You all look distressed.

461
00:19:34,256 --> 00:19:36,717
Yeah!
Your dumb machine's distressing!

462
00:19:36,801 --> 00:19:38,344
[groans]
It's like it emits shame.

463
00:19:38,427 --> 00:19:41,180
What did you expect
from a dungeon treadmill?

464
00:19:41,263 --> 00:19:44,850
Regardless, I might be able
to soothe some of your concerns.

465
00:19:44,934 --> 00:19:46,852
All with the simple push
of a button.

466
00:19:46,936 --> 00:19:48,104
[machine beeps]

467
00:19:48,187 --> 00:19:50,064
-Oh, that smells nice.
-Thank you.

468
00:19:50,147 --> 00:19:52,233
I designed it
with a relaxing aroma function.

469
00:19:52,316 --> 00:19:54,985
[KOUSUKE] I admit,
it really is quite calming.

470
00:19:55,069 --> 00:19:56,779
[NANAMI] It's mixed
from Nanami essence.

471
00:19:56,862 --> 00:19:58,656
The hell even is Nanami essence,

472
00:19:58,739 --> 00:20:00,157
and where did you
extract it from?

473
00:20:00,241 --> 00:20:02,660
Master, really, please don't
ask me that question.

474
00:20:02,743 --> 00:20:04,370
Oh, and now you act embarrassed.

475
00:20:05,121 --> 00:20:07,873
[NANAMI] Another helpful feature
is the climate control system.

476
00:20:08,416 --> 00:20:09,250
-[HATSUMI] Must push.
-[beeps]

477
00:20:10,835 --> 00:20:11,961
Oh, yeah, it definitely

478
00:20:12,044 --> 00:20:13,045
-got warmer.
-[growls]

479
00:20:13,838 --> 00:20:16,173
Really?! That's even dumber!

480
00:20:16,257 --> 00:20:18,801
Why would anyone want
to be blasted with hot air

481
00:20:18,884 --> 00:20:21,220
when they're already hot
from running on a treadmill?!

482
00:20:21,303 --> 00:20:23,013
[CLARIS] Please, Princess!
Try to calm yourself!

483
00:20:23,097 --> 00:20:24,557
[KOUSUKE] Huh? Should it
keep getting hotter?

484
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:25,599
[all gasp]

485
00:20:25,975 --> 00:20:28,769
[KOUSUKE] No! Too hot!
It's way too hot now!

486
00:20:28,853 --> 00:20:30,396
It's actually burning me!

487
00:20:30,479 --> 00:20:31,730
[YUKINE] Hang on, Kousuke!

488
00:20:31,814 --> 00:20:33,732
-Hit the cold air button!
-[panting]

489
00:20:33,816 --> 00:20:35,192
[HATSUMI] I don't think
that it has one.

490
00:20:35,276 --> 00:20:37,987
-Do something, anything!
-[NANAMI] As you wish.

491
00:20:38,070 --> 00:20:39,029
Huh?

492
00:20:39,530 --> 00:20:40,865
[yelps]

493
00:20:40,948 --> 00:20:41,907
[all gasp]

494
00:20:42,408 --> 00:20:44,160
[NANAMI] It casts a protection
spell over the head,

495
00:20:44,243 --> 00:20:45,828
so Master is unharmed.

496
00:20:46,745 --> 00:20:48,706
[NANAMI] I've tried it myself,
in fact.

497
00:20:48,789 --> 00:20:50,583
It was quite exhilarating.

498
00:20:50,666 --> 00:20:52,752
[LUDIVINE] Kousuke!

499
00:20:53,502 --> 00:20:54,712
Hmm.

500
00:20:54,795 --> 00:20:57,047
I saw that hole.
Should've asked about it.

501
00:20:58,090 --> 00:20:59,508
♪

502
00:21:00,134 --> 00:21:01,927
[YUKINE] Are you sure
that you don't need a doctor

503
00:21:02,011 --> 00:21:04,764
-or anything?
-[Kousuke laughs] I'm fine.

504
00:21:05,222 --> 00:21:07,141
And Nanami's not allowed
to work on the machine

505
00:21:07,224 --> 00:21:09,101
without Claris supervising her.

506
00:21:09,727 --> 00:21:10,644
Oh, good.

507
00:21:11,061 --> 00:21:12,897
Just think of all the lives
Claris will save.

508
00:21:13,355 --> 00:21:15,483
Anyway,
why are you putting yourself

509
00:21:15,566 --> 00:21:17,193
through the wringer like this?

510
00:21:17,276 --> 00:21:19,612
Don't you worry
you might be overdoing it?

511
00:21:19,695 --> 00:21:21,822
Rest is important too, you know.

512
00:21:21,906 --> 00:21:23,032
Says you.

513
00:21:23,365 --> 00:21:25,910
Come on, you train more
than anyone I've ever met.

514
00:21:25,993 --> 00:21:28,787
Besides, if I'm going to
become the strongest,

515
00:21:28,871 --> 00:21:31,040
then I've got a whole lot
of work to do to get there.

516
00:21:31,999 --> 00:21:33,751
And then there's
the real reason.

517
00:21:34,668 --> 00:21:36,170
But it's not like
I'm gonna tell her

518
00:21:36,253 --> 00:21:38,797
I'm doing all this to give all
the heroines a happy ending.

519
00:21:39,965 --> 00:21:41,050
[YUKINE] The strongest, huh?

520
00:21:41,133 --> 00:21:42,718
[KOUSUKE] That's the plan.

521
00:21:42,802 --> 00:21:44,512
Don't you also
wanna get stronger?

522
00:21:44,887 --> 00:21:46,096
[YUKINE] Yeah, I do.

523
00:21:46,180 --> 00:21:48,098
Then let's work
at getting stronger together!

524
00:21:49,016 --> 00:21:50,559
[chuckles] Okay!

525
00:21:50,643 --> 00:21:51,811
For starters,

526
00:21:52,102 --> 00:21:54,271
are you up for doing
a dungeon crawl with me soon?

527
00:21:54,772 --> 00:21:55,731
A dungeon crawl?

528
00:21:56,357 --> 00:21:57,900
Yeah, I mean,
if you don't want to,

529
00:21:57,983 --> 00:21:59,276
-that's cool.
-No.

530
00:21:59,360 --> 00:22:01,403
As long as
I don't have any obligations,

531
00:22:01,487 --> 00:22:02,446
I'm up for it.

532
00:22:04,156 --> 00:22:05,241
[chuckles]

533
00:22:05,908 --> 00:22:07,243
Then the crawl is on!

534
00:22:09,703 --> 00:22:11,705
[♪ closing theme song playing]

